CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --show-goto-functions
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^.*std::optional<signed_int>::optional\(this,rref_signed_int\).*$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
--
C++20 std::optional copy-initialization from a value
(`std::optional<int> o = 42;`).

This verifies the frontend selects std::optional's converting
constructor `optional(_Up&&)` and constructs the contained value.

Verified at the goto-program level rather than via full BMC: a
correctly-elaborated `std::optional<int>` pulls in the entire
`_Optional_base`/`_Optional_payload` instantiation graph, which
exceeds symbolic-execution memory limits (this is why the C++17
counterpart, cpp17_optional_basic, is also checked at the goto
level).  The goto-level check confirms the converting constructor
is actually invoked with the `int&&` value.
